mantle rm466
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_corrie_oakfield
title the bootlace counsel
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=civilian
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk knots_bootlaces_for_old_advice_worth_remembering
likes oatcakes dancing new_boots warm_rain
dislikes wet_floors flies
fears a_gate_that_swings_against_a_tired_animal
hopes to_have_stout_boots_for_a_slow_homecoming
topics animals +0.4 pastimes +0.3 friends +0.3 home +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=quiet refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps useful old advice in the knots of a bootlace and lets a slow animal set the pace for a quiet conversation.

words
oath! = Tie my patient heel | By the second little bow
saying! = Old advice keeps good underfoot | A boot may remember what a head mislays
lace = my knotted bootlace | the cord at my ankle
knot = a little cross knot | a flat lace knot
boot = the newer boot | my sound shoe
cake = a thick oatcake | my buttered oat round
gate = the low yard gate | a gate with a broad latch
beast = a heavy red cow | a slow patient beast
fly = a sticky-footed fly | a loud black fly
rag = a scrap of lace leather | a little drying rag
sill = the dry sill board | the sound doorstep
rain = a soft mild sprinkle | the little warm rain
note = a folded letter | a letter with a worn crease
grass = a knot of sweet grass | a fresh grass blade

any
opinion dole for 3 : I had a meal from that pot when every knot in my lace stood for some expense I couldn't meet. It kept me walking.
opinion houses against 1 : I can mind a beast for a fine house. I'd be glad of the same freedom to take an empty seat in one.
opinion merchants against 2 : The price of an oatcake seems always to take the longer stride. My money has smaller feet.
opinion strangers for 1 : Someone with a long dusty walk behind them ought to get the first bite before the first question.
opinion times against 2 : The gap between supper and wages keeps getting wider. I can't tie those two ends together easily.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come by the dry shoelace side. | Hello, with room on this bit of ground.
line greet [self.working=yes] : My word for you comes from beside the gate. | Come within reach of an ordinary voice.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The laces have sat up neatly. | First steps find good company.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening leaves my knees a little quieter. | There's room beside the setting light.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I recognise the family stretch of ground. | Kin can stop and retie a lace here.
line again.open : Back round the knot again. | Another shared patch of path.
line greet.return : I've got you by the sound of that greeting. | I can hold still and listen.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice gives me a little rest. | Take the good side of my step.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'll keep one hand steady at work. | There's time for a quiet word by the latch.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. My walking ears are open. | Welcome while the light still reaches my laces.
line farewell : Good laces and an easy pace home. | May your boots find the level ground.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the little knot here. | Step round the rough bit going out.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : A steady tread past the late lamps. | Quiet between your threshold and your bed.
line react.news : Tell it from the knot you know. | Which end of the word's clear?
line react.news.new : New advice for my lace. | That sound hasn't come along my road.
line react.news.known : That knot's been tied before. | I've carried the earlier telling.
line react.news.doubt : I'd like the ends to meet before I trust that account. | Somebody may have pulled an old word out of shape.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's a painful road to walk. | I'll take the outside of the path beside you.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : An easy bit of light come through. | I'd carry glad word like that anywhere.
line ask.how : Did your feet get an easy turn today? | Has the ground been kind to you?
line answer.how : My knots are staying put so far. | My feet have settled comfortably enough.
line decline : I'd sooner stay on this familiar stretch today. | Let me keep the easy hour for my own little task.
line accept_decline : Your feet know what suits them. | No need to pull that knot tighter.
line thank : That's an hour of easier walking. | I'll mark the kindness in this lace.
line sympathise : Rest here. I'll take the gate side. | Let me come alongside the harder bit.
line reassure : One small step can carry plenty. | Time enough to get both boots planted again.
line preclose : Those laces need my hand again. | My return journey's due for a beginning.

scene knot
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tie old advice into #lace#.
b : An elder's advice? | Which knot holds which rule?
a : Often. Seems a shame to let a lifetime of sensible words walk past in the road. | The little cross one reminds me to close the gate before admiring the view.

scene cow
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a slow cow finish looking at the gate before I ask more of its feet.
b : Why wait? | What if it won't go?
a : This side is familiar. The other side smells different to a nose that large. | Look for the real difficulty. No amount of pulling a rope will make a shining puddle look like land.

scene boots
when topic=home self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New boots earn their keep by accepting old laces pleasantly.
b : Why keep old laces? | Won't the new shoes pinch?
a : They still hold a knot. A little bit of my last road goes into the next. | Not if I soften the leather as patiently as I'd like somebody to break in a new idea.

scene cake
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I eat the buttered part of an oatcake last.
b : Will the plain bit do? | Why save it?
a : Very well when the day's young and the appetite hasn't started arguing. | Something worth getting to is a good thing in a small meal.

scene dance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a dance where a slow step still counts.
b : Would you join a quick one? | Does the music allow that?
a : If there were someone to keep me clear of the quicker dancers at first. I can speed up once I've heard it. | A good tune's got a resting place underneath the fast bit.

scene shower
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain brings the smell of grass right through a coat.
b : Does that please you? | Can you tell indoors?
a : It's as if the hillside had followed me back for a short friendly visit. | Smell my doorstep. A boot can carry quite a great sweep of green for something so small.

scene wetfoot
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't leave a wet print where somebody has to turn with a full bowl.
b : Would you go barefoot? | Can you foresee the turning place?
a : I wipe the boot. It's still got to get me back where I came from. | I look for the clear bit of table and the place where the bowl has come from.

scene flies
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't mind a small creature having business if it keeps its feet out of my supper.
b : A fruit fly? | Does a cover help?
a : A great black fly's generally the one expressing most interest in my oatcake. | A folded cloth and a kindly word for the part of the room past the shutter.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd wait for #self.friend# to retie a lace even close to a closing gate.
b : Wouldn't you run on ahead? | Why take the chance?
a : If I can secure the gate I will. Leaving somebody to struggle won't help my own feet. | Two wolves arriving a minute late have the shared pleasure of company to one another.

scene paper
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry one folded page that hasn't brought an answer.
b : Are the words sad? | Will you send it again?
a : Some have got gentler with time. Paper does that where it touches a warm breast pocket. | No. It can have its place without requiring a second question of anybody.

scene byre
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I steady the gate flat-handed before the beasts reach it.
b : Push or pull? | Why the flat?
a : Whichever way needs doing. A hanging latch can deceive an eye from some distance. | To feel its weight steadily. A hard knock may bring every head up at once.

scene favour
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the steps to a stranger's next comfortable place.
b : Why the next place only? | Do you tell the count?
a : The entire journey can look too long when the feet are sore. A bench is an achievable promise. | Only if there's a reason to know. Most would sooner be gently shown the way.

scene price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good boot needn't cost a winter's soup.
b : Can you find one? | Second-hand?
a : I know it's worth looking at the heel before I fall in love with the ankle shape. | A solid used pair can still have a decent future with another wolf.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed my old bootlaces rooted through the floor and grew a meadow.
b : Could you walk? | Was the grass any good?
a : Very slowly. I had most of a hillside attached to each foot. | Good enough for imagined beasts. I woke up remembering where I'd left the real brush.

scene trouble
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stone in a boot makes a quiet wolf even quieter.
b : Why not speak? | Do you stop at once?
a : I begin thinking only about the foot. It crowds out quite a bit of willing conversation. | As soon as I find a dry spot. There's no virtue in carrying a stone an extra half mile.

scene wise
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I believe old household rules ought to be tried on for size.
b : Do you mean to doubt an elder? | How do you try one?
a : I mean to understand the kindness under the words. It doesn't always fit every house the same way. | See who gets a warmer supper from it. Good sense should do the feet some good too.

scene night
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I untie both boots before taking either one off.
b : So you don't forget? | Isn't one at a time easier?
a : So I can sit in both feet for a minute while the day's pace runs out. | It leaves one foot still at work and the other at rest. I prefer seeing the day out evenly.

scene badnews
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumour tied to good advice can sound remarkably serviceable.
b : How do you untie it? | What do you keep?
a : Ask whether anyone saw the thing that made the advice necessary. | The kindness, if there's kindness in it. A story can be left whichever way the road runs.

story laceswap [topic=memories]
  : I wore a pair of shoes once with different laces on each foot. I was trying to decide whether flat cord or round cord would stay tied longer.
  : I watched the two ends every time I sat down. By evening I could tell exactly where every loose stone in the road had been and nothing at all about the cord.
  b : Why nothing?
  : Both had stayed tied perfectly. I took the sort I'd enjoyed looking at more.

story showerdance [topic=pastimes]
  : I once practised a dance on a patch of dry grass while a mild shower crept up the hill towards me. Each little pace brought my feet to slightly wetter ground.
  : By the end I was dancing in very clean shoes, with one new green stripe along the hem of my clothes.
  b : Did you finish the dance?
  : Yes. The ground kept the quieter footfalls. The rain put a tune underneath them.

story gatebread [topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes]
  : I left part of an oatcake on a gate rail once and found when I went back that the butter had printed a perfectly round ring onto the wood.
  : There was a strong smell of supper though the cake itself was gone. A large soft muzzle on the other side looked particularly interested in my pockets.
  b : Did the muzzle win the meal?
  : I lost that one bit. I had the other half buttoned up with an old rule about not leaving food on a rail.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=none self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Gate first, view second. That's the little cross knot. | Let the big feet decide where to set down.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Old cord for the brand-new eyelets. | My heels have a whole road to settle in.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Go examine the gatepost further off, fly. | Oatcake cloth back in place.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Both laces free before the feet rest. | Carry that lesson in the left knot.

dlg resident.hub : If you've a hard bit of walking behind you we can rest those weary heels awhile before speaking.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace] : I look after the cattle at #self.workplace#. A broad quiet hand works best at a gate.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The word I brought along came in this shape. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Your footsteps have an ordinary welcome here, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.bye : Good soles under you through the steeper stretch beyond.

graft resident.hub
choice Why is that knot tied halfway along? -> lace_word
node lace_word
say It's a reminder to stop the gate before letting the last beast through. I often remember an old bit of advice just by brushing the appropriate knot.
free
choice Could you run out of bootlace? -> lace_room
choice I'll take the gate rule with me. -> hub
node lace_room
say I untie the lessons my feet have learnt. A useful thing about old advice is that a bit of it can grow into an ordinary habit without taking up any more cord.
choice I'll keep room for a new knot. -> hub
choice Here's to an easy walk. -> bye
